{"metadata":{"categoryPathComponent":"Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)","role":"project","title":"Use your first OUDS components","category":"Orange Unified Design System"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-3-use-first-components","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-discovery-3-use-first-components"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[{"chapter":"Use of first components provided by OUDS","xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 26.5","estimatedTimeInMinutes":30,"projectFiles":"OUDS-Discovery-Tutorial.zip","image":"ic_component_intro.png","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDS provides components ready to be used, specified in Figma assets and preventing users to handle tokens.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are rendered thanks to the theme in use.","type":"text"}]}],"title":"Use your first OUDS components","kind":"hero","backgroundImage":"ic_component_intro.png"},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"contentSection":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"We will work on a kind of form using main OUDS components.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Feel free to style and design things as you want.","type":"text"}]}],"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia"}],"stepsSection":[{"media":null,"type":"step","code":"tutorial-discovery-3-1.swift","runtimePreview":null,"caption":[],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"First, prepare the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContentView"},{"type":"text","text":" by adding inside it a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScrollView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"media":null,"type":"step","code":"tutorial-discovery-3-2.swift","runtimePreview":"tutorial-discovery-3-2.png","caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add such picker with three items inside."}]}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Now, let’s add radio buttons to let the user choose its gender.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The official components are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSRadio"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSRadioItem"},{"text":", but the package has also a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSRadioPicker"},{"text":" to implement quicky a group of radios.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This component can be replaced by your own.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The radio picker is defined by an array of values to display radio items associated to a tag, i.e. an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"text":" thing shared through a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Inside a picker the user can select only one value, not zero.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"media":null,"type":"step","code":"tutorial-discovery-3-3.swift","runtimePreview":"tutorial-discovery-3-3.png","caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a checkbox item with only two states.","type":"text"}]}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The radio picker is alone, it is the time to add below a checkbox. OUDS provides two components: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSCheckbox"},{"type":"text","text":" which is a simple checkbox, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSCheckboxItem"},{"type":"text","text":" which is a checkbox (duh!) with additional texts and icons."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The state of the checkbox is shared through a boolean ","type":"text"},{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In some cases you may need to use ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSCheckboxIndeterminate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSCheckboxItemIndeterminate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if you want a three-states checkbox.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choose to add an instance of "},{"code":"OUDSHorizontalDivider","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":"tutorial-discovery-3-4.png","type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"There are also components who do not have any behaviors and are here only for visual rendering, for example dividers which can be horizontal or vertical.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A divider is, in the end, a stroke with a color. You will see later, colors in OUDS have two values: a light mode value, and a dark mode value. Here the divider can have a color which can change, or not.","type":"text"}]}],"code":"tutorial-discovery-3-4.swift"},{"caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a switch item, it will be used as a trick to force the change of the color scheme for the view for our future operations.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"You will then be able to see the automatic changes of colors when you switch the color scheme.","type":"text"}]}],"runtimePreview":"tutorial-discovery-3-5.png","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With radio and checkbox, OUDS provides also switch elements (toggles). They can be alone (","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSSwitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or with texts (","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSSwitchItem","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Just like the checkbox, the switch exposes its state through a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":"tutorial-discovery-3-5.swift"},{"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSLink"},{"type":"text","text":" in the app and make it open the iOS documentation OUDS website."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":"tutorial-discovery-3-6.png","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Users may need to navigate outside the app, like, for example, opening a website. Thus the ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSLink","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" component can be integrated. It can be only with a text or also a chevron indicator.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":"tutorial-discovery-3-6.swift"},{"media":null,"code":"tutorial-discovery-3-7.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In the end, we can also add a button. Button are one of the most used components in an app and bring a lof of the power and the style of the brand.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"You can find it with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSButton"},{"text":". Such button has an appearance changing its colors, and also a style (loading or not).","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thanks to the theme, the enabled, disabled, hover, focus or pressed states are managed."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":"tutorial-discovery-3-7.png","type":"step","caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Let’s add a button with some rules: if checkbox is not checked it is disabled. When tapped, change the style of the button during 5 seconds."}]}]}],"anchor":"Add-basic-components","title":"Add basic components"}]},{"kind":"assessments","assessments":[{"type":"multiple-choice","title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Does the developer using OUDS component need to manage the look and feel of the components?","type":"text"}]}],"content":[],"choices":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes","type":"text"}]}],"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No! The components use the design specifications, i.e. tokens, thanks to the theme, to define the style they must have in all cases.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No","type":"text"}]}],"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That is the reason why the ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSThemeableView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is so important: it injects the theme as environment variable so that any component can get it to define its style."}]}]}]}],"anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding"},{"title":"Add more OUDS components","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Components can be similar to iOS native components, or can also be original and strongly related to Orange Unified Design System needs."}],"action":{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get started"}],"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-4-use-other-components","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"Get started"},"kind":"callToAction","featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial"}],"hierarchy":{"modules":[{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-1-package-and-libraries","sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-1-package-and-libraries#Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-1-package-and-libraries#Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessment"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/Import-of-the-Swift-Package-and-choose-its-libraries"},{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-2-instanciate-theme","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-2-instanciate-theme#Basic-structure-for-the-app"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-2-instanciate-theme#Check-Your-Understanding"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/Preparation-of-the-theme"},{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-3-use-first-components","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-3-use-first-components#Add-basic-components"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-3-use-first-components#Check-Your-Understanding"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/Use-of-first-components-provided-by-OUDS"},{"projects":[{"sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-4-use-other-components#Add-basic-components"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-4-use-other-components#Check-Your-Understanding"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-4-use-other-components"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/Richer-and-more-original-components-of-OUDS"},{"projects":[{"sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-5-styling-things#Use-of-tokens"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-5-styling-things#Use-of-view-modifiers"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-5-styling-things#Final-result"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-5-styling-things#Want-to-be-an-artist"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-5-styling-things#Check-Your-Understanding"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-5-styling-things"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/Typography,-view-modifiers-and-tokens"},{"projects":[{"sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-6-going-further#More-resources"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-6-going-further"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/Go-further-with-more-ressources"}],"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)","doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/$volume","doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/Use-of-first-components-provided-by-OUDS"]],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)"},"kind":"project","references":{"tutorial-discovery-3-6.swift":{"type":"file","fileName":"Content.swift","syntax":"swift","highlights":[{"line":10},{"line":11},{"line":23},{"line":24},{"line":25},{"line":26}],"fileType":"swift","identifier":"tutorial-discovery-3-6.swift","content":["import OUDSSwiftUI","import SwiftUI","","struct ContentView: View {","","    @State var selectedGender: Genders = .male","    @State var termsAccepted: Bool = false","    @State var switchToDarkMode: Bool = false","","    @Environment(\\.openURL) var openUrl","","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            OUDSRadioPicker(selection: $selectedGender,","                            radios: genderRadioValues(),","                            placement: .horizontal(false))","","            OUDSHorizontalDivider(color: .brandPrimary)","","            OUDSCheckboxItem(\"I accept the terms of use\", isOn: $termsAccepted)","","            OUDSSwitchItem(\"Switch to dark mode\", isOn: $switchToDarkMode)","","            OUDSLink(text: \"Go to the website\", indicator: .next) {","                openUrl.callAsFunction(URL(string: \"https:\/\/ios.unified-design-system.orange.com\")!)","            }","        }.preferredColorScheme(switchToDarkMode ? .dark : .light)","    }","","    \/\/ MARK: - Utils","","    enum Genders: String, Hashable {","        case male","        case female","        case nonBinary","    }","","    func genderRadioValues() -> [OUDSRadioPickerData<Genders>] {","        [","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.male, label: \"Mr\"),","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.female, label: \"Ms\"),","            OUDSRadioPickerData(tag: Genders.nonBinary, label: \"Other\"),","        ]","    }","}"]},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-discovery-5-styling-things":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-5-styling-things","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Even if components increase the identity of your apps, it is not enough. Typography, fonts and tokens are here to improve that."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-discovery-5-styling-things","role":"project","title":"Styling things","kind":"project","estimatedTime":"30min"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-discovery-1-package-and-libraries#Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries":{"type":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-1-package-and-libraries#Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS iOS is exposed through an open source Swift Package hosted on GitHub, and provides several libraries for your needs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"These libraries help to split products and make users able to select only what they need."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"SwiftUI is the only official supported framework for Apple platforms.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-discovery-1-package-and-libraries#Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries","kind":"section","title":"Import the Swift Package and the libraries","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"ic_component_intro.png":{"type":"image","identifier":"ic_component_intro.png","alt":"OUDS components logo","variants":[{"traits":["1x","light"],"url":"\/images\/OUDSThemesContract\/ic_component_intro.png"}]},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)/Use-of-first-components-provided-by-OUDS":{"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Use of first components provided by OUDS","url":"\/tutorials\/table-of-contents-(discovery)\/use-of-first-components-provided-by-ouds","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/Use-of-first-components-provided-by-OUDS"},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/OUDSThemesContract/tutorial-discovery-1-package-and-libraries#Check-Your-Understanding":{"title":"Check Your Understanding","type":"link","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-discovery-1-package-and-libraries#Check-Your-Understanding","url":"\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-discovery-1-package-and-libraries#Check-Your-Understanding","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Check Your Understanding"}]},"doc://OUDSThemesContract/tutorials/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)/Richer-and-more-original-components-of-OUDS":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(discovery)\/Richer-and-more-original-components-of-OUDS","abstract":[],"url":"\/tutorials\/table-of-contents-(discovery)\/richer-and-more-original-components-of-ouds","kind":"article","ti